      "side": 1,
      "message": "This code is given \"any node below `/ietf-subscribed-notifications:filters`\" as the input `changeNode`, right? If that\u0027s the case, then the name comparison must be performed using either a (namespace, name) pair, or via an absolute XPath. Comparing node name only might match on a node such as `/ietf-subscribed-notifications:filters/stream-filter[name\u003d...]/stream-subtree-filter/example:stream-filter`.\n\nHmm, and I think that one actually *has* to perform a full ancestry check because the user might build a filter which matches the XPath of some filter, e.g., a subtree filter which targets some node below `/ietf-subscribed-notifications:filters/stream-filter` (maybe on itself, which will do the right thing accidentally, maybe some other node). If that happens, and you\u0027re walking up the tree, you want to stop the \"upper\" node, not in the node that matches inside the filter subtree.\n\nA test for this is going to be very yummy. I\u0027m already looking forward to the very long XPaths :(.",
